1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,533
What exactly did I do to tick you off?

2
00:00:03,633 --> 00:00:05,100
Did I do something wrong?

3
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:11,900
I should be the one asking you that.

4
00:00:12,533 --> 00:00:14,167
Why do you think?

5
00:00:14,267 --> 00:00:17,800
"Why do you think?"

6
00:00:19,367 --> 00:00:21,333
I'm the one asking you.

7
00:00:23,333 --> 00:00:25,033
Let's clear the air.

8
00:00:26,933 --> 00:00:29,000
Clear the air?

9
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:30,267
Yeah.

10
00:00:30,933 --> 00:00:32,767
Just spit it out.

11
00:00:39,667 --> 00:00:41,267
What, you wanna fight?

12
00:00:54,033 --> 00:00:55,533
Let me tell you right now.

13
00:00:55,633 --> 00:00:57,473
If you keep this up, I
won't back down either.

14
00:01:18,400 --> 00:01:19,633
(Yama-no-michi Police Station)

15
00:01:24,333 --> 00:01:25,933
What is your problem?

16
00:01:26,967 --> 00:01:30,533
So, why do you think?

17
00:01:54,067 --> 00:01:55,667
Takoi-san, what's wrong?

18
00:01:55,767 --> 00:01:56,167
Huh?

19
00:01:56,267 --> 00:01:59,067
Are you okay? Your voice sounds weird.

20
00:02:04,767 --> 00:02:07,100
A bug! There's a bug!

21
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:08,667
A huge one!

22
00:02:09,267 --> 00:02:10,467
A bug?

23
00:02:12,133 --> 00:02:13,433
It's massive.

24
00:02:14,033 --> 00:02:16,367
And hairy.

25
00:02:16,467 --> 00:02:17,600
With really long legs.

26
00:02:17,700 --> 00:02:19,167
What's going on?

27
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:21,467
It's a bug.

28
00:02:21,567 --> 00:02:24,633
One of those hairy ones with long legs.

29
00:02:24,733 --> 00:02:25,567
A bug?

30
00:02:25,667 --> 00:02:27,667
Yeah, I guess so...?

31
00:02:27,767 --> 00:02:30,333
Ah, yeah.

32
00:02:32,933 --> 00:02:34,600
So it was a bug.

33
00:02:35,067 --> 00:02:36,567
I see.

34
00:02:36,667 --> 00:02:39,067
We need to catch it quick.

35
00:03:01,233 --> 00:03:02,533
What are you doing?

36
00:03:03,167 --> 00:03:07,367
Nothing, I'm just curious
what kind of bug it is.

37
00:03:12,333 --> 00:03:14,467
You could have at least
come up with a better excuse.

38
00:03:25,100 --> 00:03:26,433
Hey.

39
00:03:28,733 --> 00:03:31,200
Are you messing with me?

40
00:03:31,300 --> 00:03:32,533
Yeah.

41
00:03:32,633 --> 00:03:34,273
You're playing a prank on me, aren't you?

42
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:38,867
Hey.

43
00:03:41,467 --> 00:03:43,600
Hey, at least give me a reason.

44
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:48,433
Don't tell me it's that?

45
00:03:48,533 --> 00:03:50,000
Was that supposed to be a greeting?

46
00:03:50,767 --> 00:03:53,867
Wait, didn't you grow up overseas?

47
00:03:53,967 --> 00:03:57,400
Ah, no wonder you did that. Makes sense.

48
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:00,767
It's just common sense, isn't it?

49
00:04:02,900 --> 00:04:05,300
There's only one reason, right?

50
00:04:05,400 --> 00:04:06,867
Because I wanted to kiss you.

51
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:13,133
One?

52
00:04:15,567 --> 00:04:16,867
Huh?

53
00:04:45,900 --> 00:04:49,433
"Duty First, Kiss Later"

54
00:04:50,333 --> 00:04:53,867
(Episode 2)

55
00:04:53,967 --> 00:04:55,100
Takoi-san.

56
00:04:56,700 --> 00:04:57,733
Oh!

57
00:04:57,833 --> 00:04:59,000
What a coincidence.

58
00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:01,133
I can't believe I ran into you here.

59
00:05:01,233 --> 00:05:02,467
Yeah, what a coincidence.

60
00:05:02,567 --> 00:05:04,467
Did you just get off work?

61
00:05:04,567 --> 00:05:05,767
Yeah.

62
00:05:06,167 --> 00:05:07,667
You too, Haruka?

63
00:05:07,767 --> 00:05:09,667
I just finished shopping
and I'm heading home.

64
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:11,100
Ah.

65
00:05:22,467 --> 00:05:24,900
I'm really sorry about last time.

66
00:05:25,767 --> 00:05:26,767
Don't worry about it.

67
00:05:26,826 --> 00:05:29,593
I should be the one apologizing.
Sorry for scaring you.

68
00:05:29,700 --> 00:05:32,500
I told my grandpa
that it would cause you trouble.

69
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:35,733
But he insisted
on meeting you in person.

70
00:05:36,133 --> 00:05:38,267
He's just stubborn like that.

71
00:05:40,567 --> 00:05:41,567
Ah, sorry.

72
00:05:41,667 --> 00:05:43,476
I couldn't help but use
my usual nickname for him.

73
00:05:43,500 --> 00:05:45,700
That's a bit too intimate, isn't it?

74
00:05:45,800 --> 00:05:46,600
I finally understand.

75
00:05:46,700 --> 00:05:49,433
Why my grandpa wanted to introduce
Takoi-san to me so badly.

76
00:05:49,533 --> 00:05:50,667
Huh?

77
00:05:51,500 --> 00:05:54,967
Could we exchange contact info this time?

78
00:05:55,067 --> 00:05:56,800
Ah, sure.

79
00:05:58,067 --> 00:05:59,567
I'll scan your code then.

80
00:05:59,667 --> 00:06:00,833
Okay.

81
00:06:03,633 --> 00:06:04,400
Alright, all set.

82
00:06:04,500 --> 00:06:05,767
Great.

83
00:06:07,233 --> 00:06:08,800
Thank you.

84
00:06:08,900 --> 00:06:10,300
No, thank you.

85
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:12,367
Tako-chan.

86
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:20,000
I'm heading to the shop. See you later.

87
00:06:20,100 --> 00:06:22,533
Wait... hold on, I'm coming right now.

88
00:06:24,033 --> 00:06:25,100
I'll be going then.

89
00:06:25,200 --> 00:06:26,500
Okay.

90
00:06:26,600 --> 00:06:27,933
Wait up!

91
00:06:28,033 --> 00:06:30,700
What are you doing?

92
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:32,267
What does it matter?

93
00:06:32,367 --> 00:06:34,933
We can just go together later.

94
00:06:35,300 --> 00:06:36,700
Let's go, let's go.

95
00:06:50,033 --> 00:06:51,233
This is Yamada Haruka.

96
00:06:51,333 --> 00:06:53,767
It was great seeing you today.

97
00:06:55,333 --> 00:06:56,867
That's from the girl just now, right?

98
00:06:56,967 --> 00:06:59,133
Hey, don't go snooping.

99
00:06:59,233 --> 00:07:00,500
Did you get a girlfriend?

100
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:01,467
No, it's not like that.
Not yet, not yet.

101
00:07:02,467 --> 00:07:04,900
"Not yet, not yet."

102
00:07:05,267 --> 00:07:08,267
Is she someone you can get serious with?

103
00:07:08,767 --> 00:07:12,367
Maybe she will be.

104
00:07:13,733 --> 00:07:15,767
I'm definitely going to win her over.

105
00:07:16,233 --> 00:07:18,300
Thanks for waiting, here's the fried kisu.

106
00:07:18,400 --> 00:07:19,767
Go for it.

107
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:23,733
Kisu.

108
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:36,833
We need to get things straight.

109
00:07:37,800 --> 00:07:39,200
Get what straight?

110
00:07:40,500 --> 00:07:42,267
What's wrong with you?

111
00:07:43,133 --> 00:07:44,500
Do you want some?

112
00:07:45,267 --> 00:07:46,933
Alright, I'll share one with you.

113
00:07:52,167 --> 00:07:54,167
Seriously, don't break your mother's heart.

114
00:07:54,267 --> 00:07:55,600
I'm keeping my promise.

115
00:07:55,700 --> 00:07:56,800
Let's go then.

116
00:07:56,900 --> 00:07:58,567
Alright, let's head out.

117
00:07:58,667 --> 00:08:00,167
Go straight home, okay?

118
00:08:00,533 --> 00:08:01,833
Yeah.

119
00:08:06,367 --> 00:08:07,467
Hmm?

120
00:08:07,567 --> 00:08:08,767
What's this?

121
00:08:08,867 --> 00:08:10,567
Someone just dropped it off.

122
00:08:10,667 --> 00:08:12,300
Huh? Who sent it?

123
00:08:14,900 --> 00:08:16,467
Huh? What's wrong?

124
00:08:27,267 --> 00:08:31,133
"Eat something nutritious.
Good luck with work! - Haruka."

125
00:08:39,833 --> 00:08:41,300
That's amazing.

126
00:08:46,833 --> 00:08:49,433
She even signed her name.

127
00:08:49,533 --> 00:08:51,100
That's love right there, love.

128
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:53,067
Takoi Heisuke?

129
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:55,067
Did you tell her my name?

130
00:08:55,167 --> 00:08:55,733
You mean Heisuke?
Yeah.

131
00:08:56,467 --> 00:08:58,567
Don't tell me... Why?

132
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:01,767
I never even mentioned it to her.

133
00:09:06,467 --> 00:09:08,533
That looks delicious.

134
00:09:15,667 --> 00:09:17,133
How did she know?

135
00:09:57,133 --> 00:09:58,533
Kamekichi!

136
00:10:02,033 --> 00:10:04,300
Kamekichi...?

137
00:10:11,633 --> 00:10:13,600
So you were the one making that noise.

138
00:10:15,100 --> 00:10:15,833
I was wondering.

139
00:10:15,933 --> 00:10:18,333
Why I kept hearing that rustling sound.

140
00:10:19,100 --> 00:10:20,500
I'm sorry.

141
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:22,200
I've been keeping a close eye on him.

142
00:10:22,300 --> 00:10:23,600
But Kamekichi sneaked out again.

143
00:10:23,700 --> 00:10:27,033
It's fine, no big deal.

144
00:10:30,833 --> 00:10:32,233
I'm actually a bit surprised.

145
00:10:32,867 --> 00:10:34,433
I didn't expect you to keep a turtle.

146
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,767
You know those turtle scooping games?

147
00:10:38,867 --> 00:10:39,947
Like at festivals or fairs.

148
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:41,533
Ah, yeah.

149
00:10:42,533 --> 00:10:45,767
When I was a kid, my older
sisters brought him home.

150
00:10:45,867 --> 00:10:48,100
And then dumped the job
of taking care of him on me.

151
00:10:48,200 --> 00:10:50,833
Since then, I've pretty much
been the one raising him.

152
00:10:53,733 --> 00:10:56,200
When I moved here, my mom
told me to bring him along.

153
00:10:56,300 --> 00:10:58,567
It's been over twenty years.

154
00:10:58,667 --> 00:11:00,400
Over twenty years?

155
00:11:00,900 --> 00:11:03,900
I heard turtles can
live up to thirty years.

156
00:11:04,267 --> 00:11:05,367
Seriously?

157
00:11:05,467 --> 00:11:07,400
Turtles have crazy long lifespans.

158
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:10,367
Assuming you take
good care of them, that is.

159
00:11:11,700 --> 00:11:13,233
All done.

160
00:11:20,900 --> 00:11:22,767
Pretty clean now, right?

161
00:11:23,233 --> 00:11:24,733
Right?

162
00:11:32,500 --> 00:11:33,867
Am I the kind of guy...

163
00:11:34,433 --> 00:11:36,567
who's just nice to everyone?

164
00:11:38,067 --> 00:11:39,433
Huh?

165
00:11:39,533 --> 00:11:42,300
Don't "Huh?" me, you're
the one who said it.

166
00:11:43,200 --> 00:11:45,000
So you've been dwelling on that?

167
00:11:48,033 --> 00:11:51,133
Someone else told me that before.

168
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:53,633
An ex-girlfriend?

169
00:11:56,633 --> 00:11:58,167
Hit the nail on the head?

170
00:12:01,167 --> 00:12:02,633
Because she was important to me.

171
00:12:02,733 --> 00:12:05,800
Of course I'd be nice to the person I like.

172
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:09,133
But then I got chewed out
for it. Who can stand that?

173
00:12:11,833 --> 00:12:14,667
I was just acting like I normally do.

174
00:12:17,100 --> 00:12:18,700
Like you normally do, huh...

175
00:12:23,667 --> 00:12:26,167
I can actually understand how your ex felt.

176
00:12:26,267 --> 00:12:27,267
What?

177
00:12:27,867 --> 00:12:28,867
Why?

178
00:12:28,900 --> 00:12:31,600
Of course she'd be pissed.

179
00:12:31,700 --> 00:12:35,167
For someone who desperately wanted to be
Takoi-san's most important person.

180
00:12:38,500 --> 00:12:40,000
Most important person?

181
00:12:41,833 --> 00:12:45,867
She liked how gentle Takoi-san is
with everyone.

182
00:12:45,967 --> 00:12:48,847
But the thought that he isn't like
that only with her would piss her off.

183
00:12:49,633 --> 00:12:52,333
That's probably what was
going through her mind.

184
00:12:56,833 --> 00:12:58,100
I see.

185
00:13:01,367 --> 00:13:02,867
I'm taking off.

186
00:13:03,433 --> 00:13:05,433
So, are you going to date that person?

187
00:13:06,200 --> 00:13:07,700
I don't know yet.

188
00:13:09,867 --> 00:13:11,300
Why?

189
00:13:12,900 --> 00:13:14,100
Nothing.

190
00:13:14,867 --> 00:13:17,500
If Takoi-san thinks it's a
good fit, I have no objections.

191
00:13:19,833 --> 00:13:22,700
Is that right?

192
00:13:36,300 --> 00:13:37,700
Of course she'd be pissed.

193
00:13:37,800 --> 00:13:40,760
For someone who desperately wanted to be
Takoi-san's most important person.

194
00:13:47,833 --> 00:13:50,333
As long as you're happy with it.

195
00:13:55,933 --> 00:13:58,300
(Yama-no-michi Road Police Station)

196
00:14:05,233 --> 00:14:06,033
Huh?

197
00:14:06,133 --> 00:14:08,653
Is something going on with the
Community Safety Division today?

198
00:14:08,967 --> 00:14:11,700
Ah, you mean Shiono.

199
00:14:11,800 --> 00:14:13,600
I heard he got called in.

200
00:14:13,933 --> 00:14:16,167
Huh? Why Shiono?

201
00:14:16,667 --> 00:14:17,667
Huh?

202
00:14:17,767 --> 00:14:20,533
I never even mentioned Shiono.

203
00:14:21,933 --> 00:14:24,767
Really? My bad.

204
00:14:54,600 --> 00:14:55,867
Welcome home.

205
00:14:57,733 --> 00:14:58,900
Haruka-san?

206
00:14:59,267 --> 00:15:01,733
Huh? What are you doing here?

207
00:15:02,333 --> 00:15:04,900
I couldn't get a hold of you,

208
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:06,700
so I just came straight here.

209
00:15:07,033 --> 00:15:08,153
You just came straight here?

210
00:15:08,233 --> 00:15:09,933
You haven't had dinner yet, right?

211
00:15:10,033 --> 00:15:11,033
I'll make you something.

212
00:15:11,133 --> 00:15:13,600
N-No, wait, how did you...

213
00:15:13,700 --> 00:15:15,133
Huh?

214
00:15:15,433 --> 00:15:18,667
How do you know where I live?

215
00:15:20,867 --> 00:15:21,867
Huh?

216
00:15:22,600 --> 00:15:24,400
Huh?

217
00:15:24,500 --> 00:15:29,500
I don't care who Takoi-san is nice to.

218
00:15:33,367 --> 00:15:36,667
I'm not like your ex-girlfriend.

219
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:41,333
Because she's someone
important to you, someone you like.

220
00:15:41,767 --> 00:15:44,833
And you still got yelled
at. Isn't that ridiculous?

221
00:15:51,833 --> 00:15:52,633
How do you know that?

222
00:15:52,733 --> 00:15:56,333
I just like how Takoi-san is
so gentle with everyone.

223
00:15:59,967 --> 00:16:00,600
Like?

224
00:16:00,700 --> 00:16:01,933
Yes.

225
00:16:11,433 --> 00:16:12,733
Good evening.

226
00:16:14,100 --> 00:16:15,400
Hello.

227
00:16:18,367 --> 00:16:20,467
Come on in.

228
00:16:20,567 --> 00:16:22,633
N-No, that's too...

229
00:16:22,933 --> 00:16:25,000
What's the big deal? Come on in.

230
00:16:25,100 --> 00:16:29,133
You two sure got close
fast for having just met.

231
00:16:32,167 --> 00:16:35,700
By the way, Takoi-san,

232
00:16:35,800 --> 00:16:37,867
did you buy the drinks?

233
00:16:38,767 --> 00:16:39,333
Huh?

234
00:16:39,433 --> 00:16:42,533
Didn't we agree to drink
at my place today?

235
00:16:42,633 --> 00:16:44,667
Didn't I ask you to pick
up some booze on the way?

236
00:16:52,933 --> 00:16:57,000
Oh, crap, I forgot.

237
00:16:57,100 --> 00:16:58,700
You're so unreliable.

238
00:16:59,400 --> 00:17:03,200
I guess we'll just have to make
do with what I have at home.

239
00:17:06,733 --> 00:17:09,867
In that case, I'm sorry,
but I'll just...

240
00:17:09,967 --> 00:17:11,333
I get it.

241
00:17:12,267 --> 00:17:13,467
I'll come back tomorrow.

242
00:17:13,567 --> 00:17:14,267
Huh?

243
00:17:14,367 --> 00:17:18,067
I'll make a super nutritious meal
for Heisuke-san.

244
00:17:18,500 --> 00:17:20,833
Make sure you come straight home tomorrow.

245
00:17:22,033 --> 00:17:24,400
And no stopping by the bar for drinks.

246
00:17:32,167 --> 00:17:34,267
I really don't get this woman.

247
00:17:34,533 --> 00:17:35,867
Huh?

248
00:17:35,967 --> 00:17:40,033
Didn't he say he wouldn't see you again?

249
00:17:40,300 --> 00:17:41,867
Huh?

250
00:17:41,967 --> 00:17:44,000
What's with this guy?

251
00:17:44,100 --> 00:17:44,967
So scary.

252
00:17:45,067 --> 00:17:46,500
So...

253
00:17:47,833 --> 00:17:49,200
What!

254
00:17:50,300 --> 00:17:51,933
He's mine.

255
00:17:52,033 --> 00:17:53,633
Stop flattering yourself.

256
00:17:53,733 --> 00:17:55,033
Huh?

257
00:17:55,633 --> 00:17:58,067
Whoa! Hold on...

258
00:17:58,167 --> 00:17:59,300
Wait.

259
00:18:01,767 --> 00:18:03,267
And another thing.

260
00:18:03,367 --> 00:18:06,267
I know everything about you.

261
00:18:08,233 --> 00:18:09,676
Don't ever show your face around me again.

262
00:18:09,700 --> 00:18:10,800
Get lost!

263
00:18:25,100 --> 00:18:26,633
She's gone.

264
00:18:27,133 --> 00:18:28,433
Phew...

265
00:18:31,200 --> 00:18:32,667
I looked into it.

266
00:18:32,767 --> 00:18:34,000
Huh?

267
00:18:34,300 --> 00:18:39,067
She has a history of stalking her exes
and guys she liked.

268
00:18:39,167 --> 00:18:41,067
They even filed police reports.

269
00:18:42,033 --> 00:18:43,600
Seriously?

270
00:18:44,600 --> 00:18:47,200
And she's been here many times.

271
00:18:47,300 --> 00:18:48,300
Right here.

272
00:18:48,400 --> 00:18:49,667
Huh?

273
00:18:55,933 --> 00:18:58,133
Snooping through your mailbox.

274
00:18:59,033 --> 00:19:00,400
Good work today.

275
00:19:01,133 --> 00:19:03,133
Waiting for you to get off work.

276
00:19:08,233 --> 00:19:09,733
Even following you all the way home.

277
00:19:13,800 --> 00:19:15,800
I can't believe I didn't notice.

278
00:19:16,233 --> 00:19:17,833
Are you really a cop?

279
00:19:20,533 --> 00:19:22,833
And how did you find out?

280
00:19:23,233 --> 00:19:24,700
Because I've been watching you.

281
00:19:24,800 --> 00:19:26,167
Takoi-san.

282
00:19:27,067 --> 00:19:28,833
You've been watching me?

283
00:19:28,933 --> 00:19:30,267
Yes.

284
00:19:34,900 --> 00:19:36,367
Of course I'd get jealous.

285
00:19:36,460 --> 00:19:39,193
For someone who wants to be
the most important person to Takoi-san...

286
00:19:39,700 --> 00:19:42,067
Isn't there only one reason?

287
00:19:42,167 --> 00:19:43,833
Because I want to kiss you.

288
00:19:51,400 --> 00:19:53,367
What? Ah...

289
00:19:53,467 --> 00:19:56,200
As expected of an elite.

290
00:19:56,300 --> 00:19:57,133
Yeah.

291
00:19:57,233 --> 00:19:59,109
I can't believe you
investigated that thoroughly.

292
00:19:59,133 --> 00:20:00,433
Ah!

293
00:20:00,533 --> 00:20:03,233
Is investigating your hobby or something?

294
00:20:04,433 --> 00:20:07,767
Anyway, you really saved me this time.

295
00:20:07,867 --> 00:20:09,033
Thank you.

296
00:20:15,300 --> 00:20:17,067
Who would have investigating as a hobby?

297
00:20:18,667 --> 00:20:19,533
What is wrong with you?

298
00:20:19,633 --> 00:20:21,600
I already confessed my feelings to you.

299
00:20:21,700 --> 00:20:23,780
Weren't you the one who
told me to be open about it?

300
00:20:25,500 --> 00:20:27,733
Instead of brushing me off and avoiding me,

301
00:20:27,833 --> 00:20:29,967
you should just tell me
straight up that you hate me.

302
00:20:30,067 --> 00:20:31,833
I don't hate you.

303
00:20:33,033 --> 00:20:35,067
It's not like I hate you...

304
00:20:43,233 --> 00:20:45,967
Ah, no, I...

305
00:20:46,933 --> 00:20:47,633
Takoi-san.

306
00:20:47,733 --> 00:20:48,967
Yeah.

307
00:20:50,767 --> 00:20:52,100
I like you.

308
00:20:59,333 --> 00:21:00,900
Oh, crap.

309
00:21:01,400 --> 00:21:03,833
I forgot to call my mom.

310
00:21:07,233 --> 00:21:08,600
Takoi-san.

311
00:21:11,633 --> 00:21:13,067
I really like you.

312
00:21:34,167 --> 00:21:37,567
What is wrong with me...

313
00:21:40,133 --> 00:21:41,467
Must be nice.

314
00:21:41,567 --> 00:21:43,967
The Criminal Affairs Division
looks like they're having fun.

315
00:21:44,300 --> 00:21:45,633
He's got that look on his face.

316
00:21:48,900 --> 00:21:51,133
He can't even hide his joy.

317
00:21:52,033 --> 00:21:53,500
What is wrong with me...

318
00:21:55,100 --> 00:21:56,600
To think I'd fall for Shiono.

319
00:22:02,167 --> 00:22:03,567
He's mine.

320
00:22:08,167 --> 00:22:09,567
So I guess I don't hate it.

321
00:22:24,800 --> 00:22:27,433
(This story is purely fictional.)

322
00:22:28,067 --> 00:22:30,867
(Next Episode Preview)
What on earth is going on...

323
00:22:31,667 --> 00:22:33,367
Can you say it's absolutely impossible?

324
00:22:33,467 --> 00:22:34,876
It's not like you guys are dating anyway.

325
00:22:34,900 --> 00:22:36,300
What are you doing?

326
00:22:36,633 --> 00:22:37,900
Takoi-san.

327
00:22:38,533 --> 00:22:39,300
Ouch.

328
00:22:39,400 --> 00:22:41,800
What would you do if
someone confessed to you?

329
00:22:41,900 --> 00:22:42,800
Huh?
Huh?

330
00:22:43,700 --> 00:22:44,933
I'm talking about yesterday.

331
00:22:45,033 --> 00:22:46,467
I'm heading out.

332
00:22:47,100 --> 00:22:48,367
It's all my fault...
